## Local Sources ##

  - Probate Judge Office of Geneva Co.  
    P.O. Box 430  
    Geneva, AL 36340

    The courthouse is located at 200 N. Commerce street and has
    records from 1898 forward. Some records (1898–1929) have
    been damaged by floods.

  - [Emma Knox Kenan Library](https://www.genevaal.gov/library)  
    312 S. Commerce St.  
    Geneva, AL 36340

    One of the best resources for the county are the cemetery
    records compiled by Mr. and Mrs. J.R. Phipps, 1962–1972.
    A copy of the two volume set is available here and at the
    Alabama Department of Archives and History.

    The library also has the Reaper newspaper, original and on
    microfilm from about 1900 forward.

## Alabama Department of Archives and History ##

  - [Alabama Department of Archives and History](https://archives.alabama.gov/)  
    624 Washington Ave  
    Montgomery, AL 36130

## Books and Magazine ##

  - <cite>SEAGHS Magazine</cite>

    Southeast Alabama Genealogical and Historical Society  
    P. O. Box 246  
    Dothan, AL 36302–0246

  - <cite>Hartford City Cemetery, Geneva County, Alabama</cite>  
    by Mildred Stanley and Helon Cutler, 1997  

    Southeast Alabama Genealogical and Historical Society  
    P.O. Box 246  
    Dothan, AL 36302–0246

  - <cite>Geneva County, Alabama Marriage Records 1898–1930</cite>  
    by Warrine Sheppard Hathaway, 1996

  - <cite>A Geneva County Album</cite>  
    Geneva County Historical Society, 1987  
    Published by Geneva County Publications, Inc.

  - <cite>Geneva, Alabama — A History</cite>  
    by The Geneva Woman’s Club, 1987

  - <cite>Geneva County, Alabama Tomb Records Vol. 1 and 2</cite>  
    Compiled by Mr. and Mrs. J. R. Phipps, 1962–1972

  - <cite>History of Alabama and Dictionary of Alabama Biography Vol. 1</cite>  
    by Thomas McAdory Owen

    Originally published in 1921, reprinted 1978 by The Reprint Company.
    The Geneva County [article][TMO] appears on pages 644–646.

  - <cite>Northern Alabama Historical and Biographical Illustrated</cite>

    Originally published by Smith and Deland, 1888, Birmingham, Ala.
    Reprinted 1976 by The Reprint Company, Spartanburg, SC.
    The Geneva County [article][S&D] appears on pages 235–236.

## Maps ##

  - A county road map showing cemetery names and locations as
    well as township, range and section infomation is available
    from:

    [Alabama Department of Transportation][]  
    Attn: Map Sales  
    1409 Coliseum Boulevard  
    P. O. Box 36110  
    Montgomery, Alabama 36130-3050

  - The <cite>Historical Atlas of Alabama Volume II: Cemetery
    Locations by County, 3rd Edition</cite>
    contains cemetery locations for each county and can
    be purchased from the [University of Alabama][].

